    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0603" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/121: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-06T14:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1936—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Please cable any information available regarding the rumor current here that
                    the issuance of invitations for the International Sugar Conference is being
                    delayed on the ground that the United States will probably not be able to
                    support commitments that might be undertaken regarding control of production and
                    marketings of sugar.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
